{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall place the blessing.</b> As its Targum renders: ״יָת מְבָרְכַיָּא״ — the blessers." "<b>Upon Mount Gerizim.</b> Facing Mount Gerizim they turned their faces and opened with blessing: ״Blessed is the man who does not make a carved image or a molten idol,״ and so forth. All the cursed ones in the passage were first said in the language of ״Blessed,״ and afterward they turned their faces toward Mount Eival and opened with curse (Sotah 33)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:39.660531955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}